Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Rewrite MEME cloud wrapper (evidence-based gate, temp-dir
 isolation) and add sandbox tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Vendored MEME wrapper: align the shared-cloud gate with the measured envelope
(120 proteins / 30,000 aa, matching gdm_cdd_meme), agree with the Python layer via
BPS_SHARED_CLOUD, replace the fixed /tmp/bps_meme_xxxx runtime path (which collided
across concurrent runs and leaked) with an mktemp dir cleaned on exit, add a
BPS_MEME_GATE_ONLY diagnostic hook, and expose the vendored post-processing stubs
on PATH.

Tests: new test_runtime_sandbox.py proves a runaway child (memory/CPU/timeout) is
contained without killing the parent — including a real vendored-MEME signal-kill
case. Updated cloud-stability tests to the evidence-based policy: the 40-protein
family is allowed and reaches the guarded runner; only genuinely oversized input is
refused; the wrapper allows 40 and blocks 200.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
